#: scripts/main.gd:1411
msgid "If all of a region's open cells lie in one row, its crown must be in that row. That uses up the row's crown, so cross out the rest of the row. The same works for columns, and for a row that lies inside one region."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/main.gd:1413
msgid "Groups: if two regions fit entirely within two rows, their crowns use up both rows' crowns. Cross out every other cell in those rows. It works for three regions in three rows too, and for columns."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/main.gd:1415
msgid "What if? Imagine a crown in a cell. If it would rule out every open cell left in some row, column or region, that cell can't hold a crown. Cross it out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/main.gd:1416
